l[102Gsurface[110Gboth[115Gthe[119Gskill[125Gand[129Gthat[134Gprompt.[142GYou[146Gneed[151Ga[153Grule:[159Gif[162Ga[164Gskill[170Gis[173Gserved,[181Gsuppress[190Gits[194Gown[198Gsteps[204Gfrom[209Gthe[213Gprompt[220Gresults.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mThe design I'd actually build[22m[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1BDon't give skills a parallel retrieval stack. [1mDerive the skill signal from the prompt retrieval you already trust:[2C[1B[22m[K[2C[1B1.[6Gretrieve[15G+[17Grerank[24Gprompts[43G(the[48Gstrong[55Gindex:[62G1025[67Grows,[73Gwell-indexed)[2C[1B2. fo[9G each[15Gskill, count how many of its steps appear in the top-k[K[2C[1B3. skill_sc[15Gre = coverage[29G×[31Gbest_step_rerank_score[2C[1B4.[6Gserve[12Gthe[16Gskill[22Gonly[27Gif[30Git[33Gbeats[39Gthe[43Gbest[48Gprompt[55Gby[58Ga[60Gmargin[2C[1B5.[6Gsuppress that skill's[28Gstep[33Gprompts from the[50Greturned list[K[2C[2BTwo prompts from the[24Gsame[29Gskill[35Glanding[43Gin[46Gyour[51Gtop-10[58Gis[61Gfar[65Gstronger[74Gevidence[83Gthan[88Ga[90Gone-line[99G[38;2;177;185;249mrouting_description[119G[39mscoring[127G0.7[131Gagainst[139Ga[141Gquery.[148GIt[151Guses[156Gthe[160Gindex[166Gthat[171Gworks[177Ginstead[185Gof[188Gthe[192Gone[196Gthat[201Gdoesn't,[210Gneeds[216Gno[219Gseparate[228Gembedding,[239Gand[243Gscales[250Gto[2C[1Bany[7Gnumber[14Gof[17Gskills.[2C[1B[K[2C[1BIt[6Galso fails safe: with zero resolvable steps today, c[59Gverag[65G is 0 and no skill ever wins —[96Gwhich is the correct behaviour given none can[142Gbe[145Gserved.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mOrder I'd do it in[22m[K[2C[2B1. [1mFix the 7 merge conflicts in the vault[22m, then re-ingest. Unrelated to[75Gskil[80Gs, but it's corrupt data [107Gt[109Ging in your index.[K[2C[1B2.[6G[1mRepair [38;2;177;185;249mLLM Build & Tune Analyzer[39m's step references[22m,[58Gor[61Gdelete[68Gthe[72Gskill.[79GA[81Gskill[87Gpointing[96Gat[99Gdeleted[107Gprompts[115Gis[118Gworse[124Gthan[129Gno[132Gskill.[1B [3G3. [1mPopulate 2–3 skills properly[35G[22mwith[40Greal[45Gstep[50Gchains.[2C[1B4.[6G[1mThen[11G[22mbuild[17Gthe[21Gcoverage-based[36Gscoring[44G—[46Gand[50Gonly[55Gthen[60Gcan[64Gyou[68Gtell[73Gwhether[81Git[84Gworks.[1B[K[2C[1BSteps 1–3 are data, not code. Nothing about skill retrieval is testable[75Guntil[81Gthey're[89Gdone,[95Gand[99GI'd[103Gresist[110Gwriting[118Gthe[122Gretrieval[132Glogic[138Gbefore[145Gthere's[153Gsomething[163Gto[166Gretrieve.[2B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[39m [38;2;153;153;153mChurned for 1m 15s[39m[K[2B[38;2;153;153;153m※[3G[1mrecap: [22m[3mYou're reworking Capillaries' retrieval; the embedder is fixed, union-plus-Qwen3 reranking is live, and SINGLE_THRESHOLD is removed. Skills are next but all 6 are unservable, so fix the 7 merge-conflicted vault prompts and populate real skill [2C[1Bsteps before building skill retrieval. (disable recaps in /config)[2C[1B[23m[39m[K[1B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mFollow through all of these steps[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                           [1B[49m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mStarting[12Gwith[17Gstep[22G1[24G—[26Glocating[35Gthe[39Gconflicted[50Gfiles[56Gand[60Gchecking[69Gwhether[77Gthe[81Gtwo[85Gsides[91Gdiffer.[1B[K[1B  [38;2;153;153;153mRan [1m2[22m shell commands [39m[K[5C[1B[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mAll 7 have identical sides, so resolution is unambiguous[60G—[62Gno[65Gcontent[73Gdecision[82Gto[85Gmake.[91GBacking[99Gup,[103Gthen[108Gresolving.[5C[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m●[3G[39mRe-ingest the vault[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ cd[11G/home/[18Gao-[22Gn