[22m A skill's steps[42G[3mare[23m prompts in the same index. A query matching step 2 will surface both the[119Gskill[125Gand[129Gthat[134Gprompt.[142GYou[146Gneed[151Ga[153Grule:[159Gif[162Ga[164Gskill[170Gis[173Gserved,[181Gsuppress[190Gits[194Gown[198Gsteps[204Gfrom[209Gthe[213Gprompt[220Gresults.[2C[2B[1mThe design I'd actually build[43G[22m[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1BDon't give skills a parallel re[35Grieval st[45Gc[47G. [1mDerive the skill signal from the prompt retrieval you already trust:[2C[1B[22m[K[2C[1B1[6Gretri[12Gve[15G+ rerank promp[30Gs [33G       [41G  (the st[51Gong in[58Gex: 1025[67Grows,[73Gwell-indexed)[2C[1B2.[6Gfor[10Geach[15Gskill,[22Gcount[28Ghow[32Gmany[37Gof[40Gits[44Gsteps[50Gappear[57Gin[60Gthe[64Gtop-k[2C[1B3. skill_score =[20Gcover[26Gg[29G× best_step_rerank_score[K[2C[1B4. serve the skil[21G only[27Gif[30Git[33Gbeats[39Gthe[43Gbest[48Gprompt[55Gby[58Ga[60Gmargin[2C[1B5.[6Gsuppress[15Gthat[20Gskill's[28Gstep[33Gprompts[41Gfrom[46Gthe[50Greturned[59Glist[2C[1B[K[2C[1BTwo[7Gprompts[15Gfrom[20Gthe[24Gsame[29Gskill[35Glanding[43Gin[46Gyour[51Gtop-10[58Gis[61Gfar[65Gstronger[74Gevidence[83Gthan[88Ga[90Gone-line[99G[38;2;177;185;249mrouting_description[119G[39mscoring[127G0.7[131Gagainst[139Ga[141Gquery.[148GIt[151Guses[156Gthe[160Gindex[166Gthat[171Gworks[177Ginstead[185Gof[188Gthe[192Gone[196Gthat[201Gdoesn't,[210Gneeds[216Gno[219Gseparate[228Gembedding,[239Gand[243Gscales[250Gto[2C[1Bany number of skills.[2C[2BIt[6Galso fails safe: with zero resolvable steps today, coverage is 0 and[75Gno skill ever wins — which is[105Gthe correct behaviour given[133Gnone[138Gcan[142Gbe[145Gserved.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mOrder I'd do it[19Gin[22m[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1B1.[6G[1mFix the 7 merge conflicts in the vault[22m,[46Gthen[51Gre-ingest.[62GUnrelated[72Gto[75Gskills,[83Gbut[87Git's[92Gcorrupt[100Gdata[105Gsitting[113Gin[116Gyour[121Gindex.[2C[1B2. [1mRepair [38;2;177;185;249mLLM Build & Tune Analyzer[39m's step references[22m, or delete the skill. A[81Gskill pointing at[99Gdelet[105Gd prompts is[118Gworse [125Ghan no[132Gskill.[K[2C[1B3.[6G[1mPopulate 2–3 skills properly[35G[22mwith[40Greal[45Gstep[50Gchains.[1B [3G4. [1mThen[22m build the coverage-based[36Gscoring[44G—[46Gand[50Gonly[55Gthen[60Gcan[64Gyou[68Gtell[73Gwhether[81Git[84Gworks.[2B [3GSteps 1–3 are data, not code. Nothing about skill retrieval is testable until they're done, and I'd resist writing the retrieval logic before there's something to retrieve.[K[2C[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GChurned for 1m 15s[1B[39m[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m※[3G[1mrecap: [22m[3mYou're reworking Capillaries' retrieval; the embedder is fixed, union-plus-Qwen3 reranking is live, and SINGLE_THRESHOLD is removed. Skills are next but all 6 are unservable, so fix the 7 merge-conflicted vault prompts and populate real skill [1B[23m[39m [3G[38;2;153;153;153m[3msteps before building skill retrieval. (disable recaps in /config)[23m[39m[K[2B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mFollow through all of these steps[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                           [2C[2B[49mStarting with s[19Gep 1[24G— locating the conflicted files and[60Gchecking wheth[75Gr the tw[85Gsid[89Gs[91Gdiffer.[99G[K[6C[2B[38;2;153;153;153m[1m2[2C[2B[22m[39mAll 7 have [15Gden[19Gical sid[28Gs, so[34Gresolution [46Gs unambiguous — no content d[75Gcision to make. Backing[99Gup,[103Gthen[108Gresolving.[2B [3G[38;2;153;153;153mRan [1m4[22m shell commands [25G[39m[K[1B[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mBefore running this — checking whether