75Gwork.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mNot on the branch at all — database state[22m[K[2C[1B[K[2C[1BThe skill refinement[24Gis mostly [3mdata[23m, and d[47Ga doesn't live in git:[2C[2B- 17 restored s[19Gep prompts (rows in[39G[38;2;177;185;249mprompts[39m)[K[2C[1B- [38;2;177;185;249mskills.steps[39m JSONB[24Gwiring[31Gfor[35Gall[39G6[41Gskills[2C[1B-[5GThe[9G[38;2;177;185;249mLLM Build & Tune Analyzer[35G[39mrepair[2C[1B- [38;2;177;185;249mprompts.exact_tsv[39m, the[28G[38;2;177;185;249mVECTOR(1024)[41G[39mmigration,[52Gevery[58Gembedding[2C[2BIf you restore[18Gthis database from[37Ga backup, or run [55G[38;2;177;185;249mnsert_prompts_batch[39m with its default [38;2;177;185;249mprune_orphans=True[39m again, all[122Gof[125Git goes and the branch won't bring it back. The[173Gonl[177G [180Gpr[183Gducible[191Gparts[198Gre[201Gthe sch[209Gma[212G([38;2;177;185;249mdb/setup.py[39m, [38;2;177;185;249mmigrate_embed_dim.py[39m) and[252Gthe[2C[1Bingest scripts.[K[2C[2B[1mT[5Gird place — the vault[2C[2B[22mThe 7 conflict resolu[25Gions[30Gare[34Gin[37G[38;2;177;185;249m~/Documents/Obsidian/Main Vault[39m, a [1mseparate git repo on [38;2;177;185;249mmain[22m[39m. Some[104Ghing auto-commit[122Git[125G([38;2;177;185;249mc7f9d09 vault backup: 2026-08-16 20:20:25[39m), so they're committed there and[201Gno[204Gmarkers[212Gremain[219Gin[222GHEAD.[228GThat's[235Ga[237Gdifferent[247Grepo[2C[1Bfrom[8G[38;2;177;185;249mcapillaries[20G[39mand[24Gmoves[30Gindependently.[2C[1B[K[2C[1B[1mWhat I'd do[22m[K[2B [3GCommit the branch[21G—[23Git's[28Ga[30Glot[34Gof[37Guncommitted[49Gwork[54Gand[58Gseveral[66Gchanges[74Gwere[79Ghard-won[88Gcorrections[100Gthat[105Gwould[111Gbe[114Gtedious[122Gto[125Greconstruct.[138GI[140Ghaven't[148Gcommitted[158Ganything[167Gbecause[175Gyou[179Ghaven't[187Gasked[193Gme[196Gto.[2B  Worth deciding separately: whether the skill-step wiring should be reproducible from code rather than living only in Postgres. Right now [38;2;177;185;249minsert_db[39m in [38;2;177;185;249mscripts/ingest_public.py[39m still hardcodes [38;2;177;185;249msteps '[]'::jsonb[39m — I wired the steps with a one-off script,[K[2C[1Bso[6Gre-running[17Gthat[22Gingest[29Gwould[35Gempty[41Gthem[46Gagain.[53GFolding[61Gthat[66Glogic[72Ginto[77Gthe[81Gscript[88Gis[91Gthe[95Gdifference[106Gbetween[114G"fixed"[122Gand[126G"fixed[133Greproducibly."[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GBaked for 1m 1s[2C[1B[39m[K[1B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mSkill step wiring should be the same as prompt step wiring[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                  [1B[49m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mRight[9G—[11Gthat[16Gmeans[22Git[25Gbelongs[33Gin[36G[38;2;177;185;249mingest_public.py[39m,[54Gidempotent[65Gand[69Gre-runnable,[82Gnot[86Ga[88Gone-off.[97GLet[101Gme[104Gread[109Gthe[113Gcurrent[121Gskills[128Gpath.[1B[K[1B  [38;2;153;153;153mRan [1m2[22m shell commands [39m[K[5C[1B[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mNow I see it — the[22Gscript[29G[3mdoes[34G[23mtry[38Gto[41Gwire[46Gsteps,[53Gand[57Git's[62Gthe[66Gsource[73Gof[76Gthe[80Gbug[84GI[86Gfixed[92Gby[95Ghand:[101Gline[106G296[110Gsets[115G[38;2;177;185;249mprompt_id[125G[39mto[128Ga[130G[1mfilename stem[22m,[145Gnot[149Ga[151GUUID.[157GThat's[164Gexactly[172Gwhat[177G[38;2;177;185;249mLLM Build & Tune Analyzer[203G[39mhad.[208GMaking[215Git[218Gmatch[224Gthe[228Gprompt[235Gpath.[5C[1B[K[2C[1B[38;2;153;153;153mRan [1m1[22m shell command [39m[K[5C[1B[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[6G[39m[K[59;1H[57;3H[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[?25l[H[52B[38;2;215;119;