 but scoped so vault[71Grows[76Gare[80Gnever[86Gtouched.[2C[2B[1mVerified[22m[K[2C[2Brun[7G1 → md5 of public prompt ids: 9e942009020529378301e26e9a3d1df1[K[2C[1Brun[7G2[9G→[11Gmd5[15Gof[18Gpublic[25Gprompt[32Gids:[37G9e942009020529378301e26e9a3d1df1[2C[1B[K[2C[1BIdempotent, IDs stable. Final state: 1 025 prompts, 2 081 chunk[67G, [70Gl[72G [74Gmbedded, [1m6 skills wired, 0 dead step references.[22m Tests[129G102[133Gpassed[140G/[142G4[144Gfailed[151G—[153Gthe[157Gsame[162Gfour[167Ggolden[174Gfailures[183Gthroughout.[2B [3GThe state is now reproducible[33Gfrom[38Gsource:[46G[38;2;177;185;249mpython3 scripts/ingest_public.py --db-only[89G[39mrebuilds[98Gevery[104Gskill's[112Gsteps[118Gfrom[123G[38;2;177;185;249mpublic_prompts/skills/[39m.[2B  Two things still not reproducible, worth knowing: the [38;2;177;185;249mLLM Build & Tune Analyzer[39m repair lives only in the database — it's hand-authored, not in [38;2;177;185;249mpublic_prompts/[39m, so a fresh database won't have it. And [38;2;177;185;249mobsidian_sync.ingest[39m still defaults[K[2C[1B[38;2;177;185;249mprune_orphans=True[39m,[23Gwhich[29Gis[32Gwhat[37Gdeleted[45Gyour[50G67[53Gpublic[60Gprompts[68Gearlier;[77Ganyone[84Grunning[92Ga[94Gvault[100Gingest[107Ghits[112Gthat[117Gagain.[1B[K[1B[38;2;153;153;153m✻[3GCooked for 4m 54s[1B[39m[K[1B[48;2;55;55;55m[38;2;80;80;80m❯ [38;2;255;255;255mMy public prompts are only for demo purposes and should be in my Postgres public side. Obsidian shouldn't have it[39m                                                                                                                                           [5C[1B[49m[K[1B[38;2;255;255;255m●[3G[39mExactly — and that's[24Gthe[28Gbug[32Gthat[37Gbit[41Gus.[45GThe[49Gvault[55Gingest[62Gpruned[69Gthem[74Gbecause[82Gthey[87Garen't[94Gvault[100Gfiles.[107GLet[111Gme[114Gscope[120Git[123Gproperl